# Package layering (tools type packages)

## Dependency order (bottom to top)

1. `@transcend-io/type-utils` — no `@transcend-io/*` dependencies
2. `@transcend-io/internationalization` — no `@transcend-io/*` dependencies
3. `@transcend-io/airgap.js-types` — only `internationalization`, `type-utils`
4. `@transcend-io/privacy-types` — only `airgap.js-types`, `internationalization`, `type-utils`

Never add an edge that points upward (for example `airgap.js-types` → `privacy-types`). That recreates turbo build cycles and bloats the admin types barrel.

Each package has `package-dependencies.test.ts`. Update the allowlist when you intentionally add a downward dependency.

`pnpm check:packages` also runs `scripts/package-layering.test.ts`, which asserts the same allowlists at the repo root.

## Where to put a new enum or codec

Stop at the first yes:

1. Generic helper with no Transcend meaning? → `type-utils`
2. Locale key, translation primitive, or “locales product X supports” list? → `internationalization`
3. airgap.js, a customer site, or a deployed airgap bundle sees it (load options, experiences, purposes, IAB/TCF, bundle module or file names)? → `airgap.js-types`
4. Otherwise (admin, GraphQL, `transcend.yml`, DSR, assessment)? → `privacy-types`

